.TH RECT_HIT_SIDE 3 "generalGameEngine" "Engine Manual" "Engine Manual"
.SH NAME
rect_hit_side \- Given two overlapping rectangles, the side of b that a is shallowest on, i.e. the side a most likely arrived from
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include \(dqcollide.h\(dq
.BI "HitSide rect_hit_side(Rect a, Rect b);"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Given two overlapping rectangles, the side of b that a is shallowest on, i.e. the side a most likely arrived from. Decides what a collision means: a player HIT_TOP of an enemy stomps it, any other side takes damage; a ball HIT_LEFT or HIT_RIGHT of a paddle reverses its x velocity, HIT_TOP or HIT_BOTTOM its y. Only meaningful when rect_overlaps(a, b) is true. For sliding along solid tiles use tilemap_move() instead, which resolves each axis properly.
.PP
This is a static inline function; it is defined in the header.
.SH RETURN VALUE
the HitSide.
.SH MODULE
math (src/engine/math/collide.h)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rect_overlaps (3),
.BR HitSide (3),
.BR tilemap_move (3),
.BR gge\-api (7),
.BR gge (1)
